cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Dependency Analysis and Plan Obfuscator
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ayman
    family-names: El-Sayed
    email: aelsaye6@gmu.edu
    affiliation: George Mason University
abstract: >-
  Classical task planning has its application in autonomous
  systems on deciding the actions a robot should take to
  achieve a goal. Given a fully specified domain, problem,
  and goal, the agent can determine what to do based on the
  solver used. However, commonly used solvers are prone to
  producing plans that reveal intent to a passing observer.
  This is a concern in multi-agent settings that handle
  sensitive information, such as hospitals, where staff must
  respect their patients' privacy. This project develops two
  complementary capabilities: (1) dependency analysis, which
  identifies which actions have casual links, and (2) plan
  obfuscation, which restructures or augments plans to
  better hide goal-critical actions from an observer. These
  capabilities are achieved using the technical stack of
  Python scripting with the Unified Planning and Fast
  Downward libraries.
